meta {
  name: Review Seat Cancellation Request
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/college-admin/seat-cancellations/{{seatCancellationId}}/review
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{staffToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "decision": "approve",
    "remarks": "Approved per student's relocation request.",
    "refund_amount": 5000,
    "refund_status": "processed"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 200) {
    const data = res.getBody();
    console.log("Reviewed request status:", data.data && data.data.status);
  }
}

docs {
  College admin approves or rejects a pending request.

  Body:
  - decision: "approve" | "reject"
  - remarks: optional, but REQUIRED when decision is "reject"
  - refund_amount / refund_status: optional, record-keeping only (no
    automated gateway refund is issued) — refund_status is one of
    not_applicable | pending | processed | denied

  On approve, inside one transaction:
  - Enrollment.status -> "withdrawn" (this is what actually revokes
    Student Hub access — every Student Hub gate now checks
    Enrollment.status === "active")
  - ApplicationCourse.status -> "dropped_out" (+ status log entry)
  - The seat is released back to the course quota / seat pool
  - The student's BeaconU Card is deactivated
  - SeatCancellation.status -> "approved"

  The student can submit a brand-new Application for the same course at
  the same college afterward if they want to rejoin — the duplicate-course
  guard treats "dropped_out" the same as "withdrawn" (non-blocking).

  409 ConflictError if the request isn't "pending" anymore (already
  processed). 404 if the request doesn't belong to this college.
}
